float strategyInvalidationControlMin = input.float(0.50, "Opposing-control threshold", minval = 0.30, maxval = 0.90, step = 0.01, group = G_RISK,
     tooltip = "Was 0.58. SL CONTROL TRANSFER only closes once strategyLogicalConfirmCloses (=2) CONSECUTIVE bars each clear this opposing-control score - the streak resets to 0 on any bar that doesn't. In the 93-trade baseline audit (2026-05-03..2026-08-23, BTCUSDT.P 15m) the two worst SL CONTROL TRANSFER losses (-6.17 and -11.05 USD) already had adverse excursion past strategyMinInvalidationEvidenceAtr (0.30 ATR) by bar 2-4 after entry, yet did not close until bar 24 and bar 13 - the evidence threshold was not the bottleneck, the 2-consecutive-bars-at-this-control-level requirement was. Lowered from 0.58 to 0.50 to let a genuinely adverse but slightly choppy move satisfy the streak sooner. This only changes when an already-open losing trade closes - it does not touch entry admission, BUY/SELL signal generation, TP or position sizing. Re-test in Strategy Tester before assuming a dollar outcome: closing a losing trade sooner still frees the position earlier for whatever signal comes next, which changed results unpredictably the last two times an admission-side change was tried here.")
